-- title:
--   Connectedness of the place space of a complex function field
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure, and assume there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $\mathbb{C}$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\mathbb{C}(x)$ generated by $x$. Assume `IsCurveOver ℂ F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ has an associated divisor of degree $0$ whose value at each place is $\operatorname{ord}_v f$, every place has residue field finite over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\Omega[F/\mathbb{C}]$ is free of rank one over $F$. Here a place $v$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring; $\operatorname{ord}_v f$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation, and $\operatorname{evalAt} v f$ is the residue class of $f$ transported back to $\mathbb{C}$ when $f$ lies in the valuation subring, and $0$ otherwise. Suppose the set of places carries a topology and an atlas of $\mathbb{C}$-valued charts making it compact, and suppose that for every nonzero $f \in F$ and every place $v$ the chart reading $z \mapsto \operatorname{evalAt}\bigl(\varphi_v^{-1}(z)\bigr) f$, with $\varphi_v$ the extended chart at $v$ for the model $\mathbb{C}$, is meromorphic at $\varphi_v(v)$ with meromorphic order there equal to $\operatorname{ord}_v f$. Then the space of places is nonempty and connected.
--
--   This is the connectedness clause of the Riemann existence theorem for the Riemann surface attached to a function field in one variable over $\mathbb{C}$, isolated as a consequence of compactness together with the order condition on chart readings; no compatibility of the charts and no separation axiom are imposed. It is used in the construction of such a charted structure, [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_chartedSpace_meromorphicOrderAt_evalAt_eq_ord_complex`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_chartedSpace_meromorphicOrderAt_evalAt_eq_ord_complex).
